</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion and Future Work</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper presents two complementary components for efficient offline reinforcement learning: a Unified Token Representation that jointly encodes return-to-go, state, and action information to reduce sequence redundancy, and a Gated CNN Decision Module that leverages lightweight convolution to capture temporal dependencies effectively. Together, these components enable compact, scalable, and resource-efficient policy learning while maintaining strong performance across D4RL benchmarks. Notably, the Unified Token Representation also has the potential to serve as a foundational building block for future large-scale decision-making models. In future work, we plan to explore extending UTR to larger models and more complex environments, as well as integrating it with advanced modeling techniques to further improve scalability and generalization in high-dimensional decision tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
